    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As spring weather arrived, the numbers ticked up like a predictable punchline: apprehensions on the southwest border rose from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. Yet year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows, creating a grand illusion of control while federal agents and analysts watch. The real spectacle? Politicians deadlocked over funding, performing in a reconciliation farce where progress goes to die.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
