    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Lawmakers, the deadlocked performers in this reconciliation farce, remain stuck in a legislative traffic jam over separate funding for immigration enforcement. Meanwhile, on the southwest border, the numbers ticked up like a predictable punchline: a rise in apprehensions driven by spring weather. Analysts, observers of this bureaucratic yo-yo effect, point out the absurdity of the endless tug-of-war over money even as crossing statistics stay historically low.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
