    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The increase in apprehensions along the southwest border—from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March—followed milder spring weather, a statistical trend observed by security analysts. While year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows under current policies, the border security agency watches as lawmakers stay deadlocked over funding. This legislative stalemate creates a political circus where the solemn facade of low crossing numbers masks a deeper government impasse.",
